WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.110
OK, so now let's go from talking about police
to talking about destruction of property.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:11.839
There are reasonable people who have centered
in on what seems to be a dividing line as

00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:17.150
we see unrest and protests and physical violence
and property damage around the country.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.849
When we talk about property damage, there
is often a debate as to whether it counts

00:00:21.849 --> 00:00:26.750
as violence in the sense of when people say
I am against violence.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:34.379
So most people agree attacking random bystanders
who aren't being violent is unacceptable violence,

00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:38.200
attacking random police who aren't doing anything
wrong.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.790
That is violence in an in any sense of the
word.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.000
Most people agree blocking traffic is not
violence.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Now, you.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.649
Before or against blocking traffic as a protest
tactic.

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:52.680
But most people would not say blocking traffic
is violence up.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.010
You could maybe say, well, if you prevent
people from getting to work and then they

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.910
lose their jobs, blocking traffic becomes
kind of like economic violence.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.100
But in the kind of violence we're talking
about, blocking traffic.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.129
Most people agree is is not violence.

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:06.310
What about property damage?

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:10.659
So, first of all, we have to call out the
right wing hypocrites on this issue.

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:15.140
The concern trolls who a month ago were saying
sacrifice grandma to corona virus in order

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.720
to open the economy, who are now saying the
worst thing you can do is break the windows

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.890
of a big box store.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.049
They are hypocrites.

00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:25.670
I'm not interested in those hypocritical,
concerned trolls.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:31.790
I want to deal with the real people, with
the sensible people who in a real way want

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.570
to talk about this.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:39.200
There are folks who believe that, for example,
destroying government property when no one

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.259
gets physically hurt is OK.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:47.030
But for example, destroying a private business
is not OK.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.409
That depends on who you're targeting.

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:52.110
You could be targeting a business with bad
practices or you could be targeting a government

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.020
that is a bad actor or whatever.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:58.860
You could find, you know, a logging company
and say we are going to destroy or disable

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.280
their bulldozers so that they cannot take
down these trees.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.240
Saying what determines whether destruction
of property is violence is merely whether

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.670
you're doing it to a government property or
to private property.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.020
I don't think that's really the dividing line.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.770
What this comes down to is what do we mean
by violence?

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:23.940
Violence defined as behavior involving physical
force to hurt, damage or kill someone or something

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.850
damaging property even sort of fits.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:33.800
If you want to take a legal perspective, certainly
the unlawful exercise of force or the exhibition

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.630
of such force would encompass the destruction
of property.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:44.220
Now, others would say the real crux of human
violence versus physical violence against

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.590
people rather than objects is where we should
be focusing.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:55.010
If you are talking about breaking a window,
that's not really what a lot of people believe

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.480
is violence.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.880
So here's the bottom line.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:02.390
If you want to make this a semantic argument,
if you want to make this about definitions,

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:06.450
you can define violence in a way that does
or doesn't include property crime.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.190
It won't really get to the underlying issue.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:14.960
And the underlying issue is whether sometimes
violence is justified.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:22.090
So even if we agree on whether property crime
is or is not violence, that doesn't answer

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:29.960
the question of whether property crime, destruction
of property is a valid form of protest.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.420
Who gets to decide what's in the protesting
playbook?

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:40.430
If you leave the protesting playbook only
to the elites and those in positions of power,

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:46.600
it will be restricted to only writing letters,
you know, chanting and holding signs.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.600
Right.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:53.610
The point is, if you let those already in
power define what is OK in terms of protesting,

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.340
certainly nothing will ever change.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.120
Now, is there any guarantee that destroying
property is going to achieve change?

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.120
There's not.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.760
We do know that destruction of property has
been a part of protesting for a really long

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.760
time.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.510
You look at the Boston Tea Party destroyed
property to fight back against the capitalist

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:14.020
monopoly and political rights that were being
claimed by British colonists.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:19.500
You look at slave uprisings in the United
States, which included destruction of property.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:20.760
You look at the plowshares aid.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:26.900
A group of eight Christians, including priests
and nuns who took hammers to the nose cones

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:32.730
of some nuclear warheads, poured their blood
on the facility's papers and a call for peace.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:37.030
So the legality part of it is clear this stuff
is illegal to do.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:42.980
But I think we can all every single one of
us imagine a situation where we do the moderate

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.180
methods and they bring no change.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.180
They don't get attention.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:52.100
And then you say, well, we don't want to do
violence to people, but we're going to start

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.720
destroying some property destruction of property.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:05:02.680
In my mind is clearly violence of a kind,
but in certain situations, it might be the

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:08.000
only thing people have left short of starting
to actually do violence to individuals.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.650
Now, which situations count?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:10.650
I don't know.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:11.650
I don't know.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:12.650
What about the consequences?

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:13.760
Well, there are consequences.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.260
You're not going to get around that.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.400
Will property damage get you what you want?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.820
Often it will not.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.480
Property damage may, in fact, do the opposite.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:22.890
It may turn public opinion against you.

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:29.390
But whether property damage that's not hurting
anyone physically is a valid form of protest.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.690
That's a question that goes back at least
hundreds of years.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:37.730
And anybody pretending that there is one single
solitary answer that applies to every situation

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:38.730
is just wrong.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.530
History tells us that's not the case.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.700
I want to hear from you about this.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:46.030
We're going to continue covering it on The
David Pakman Show Instagram.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.961
At The David Pakman Show, we will take a break
and be back with much David Pakman show at

00:05:47.961 --> 00:05:47.970
David Pakman Dot.com.

